ctive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.4.1.stable.mono.official.49a5bc7b6\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 (build number if known) Intel HD Graphics 520 (integrated) Vulkan 1.0.66\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a resource fails to save — whether due to corruption or another issue — Godot currently displays a generic alert: \"Error saving resource!\" Unfortunately, it doesn't specify which resource failed or why, making it extremely difficult to debug in larger projects with many assets.\n\n\nThe cause is most likely\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/editor/editor_node.cpp Line 1591\n\nFrom what I’ve observed, the error dialog could be much more helpful if it included:\n\nThe full path of the resource that failed\n\nA brief explanation of the error (e.g. missing dependency, invalid format)\n\nA link to relevant documentation or a log file\n\n\nAdditionally, the affected editor_node.cpp file seems to commonly contain vague error messages that do not clearly indicate the underlying problem.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a script file:\nTodo.gd\ninsert:\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nfunc noise():\n\tvar myno : = FastNoiseLite.new()\n## todo consider fastnoise2\n```\nRename it to\nTodo.txt\n\ntry to safe it.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTry to safe a corrupt resource any project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_i